Subject: [PATCH] mm: zero freed init memory for sparse checkpoints

The 0xcc fill in freed initramfs memory is preserved in checkpoints and
causes high host memory usage during simulation.

This patch fills freed init memory with zero so emulators can use
sparse allocation for these pages.

--- a/include/linux/poison.h
+++ b/include/linux/poison.h
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
 #define	POISON_END	0xa5	/* end-byte of poisoning */
 
 /********** arch/$ARCH/mm/init.c **********/
-#define POISON_FREE_INITMEM	0xcc
+#define POISON_FREE_INITMEM	0x00
 
 /********** fs/jbd/journal.c **********/
 #define JBD_POISON_FREE		0x5b
